1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:13,919
All five cards from lessons 1–5 — full dialogues with the examiner. Plus twelve questions that fit almost every card and five mistakes that cost people points. Get ready and ask out loud!

2
00:00:14,833 --> 00:00:29,323
How does task 2 work? You get two cards with a situation. On each card you ask four questions: three from the hints and one of your own. The examiner answers. You can get twelve points in total.

3
00:00:30,233 --> 00:00:43,189
The card has only short hints. You must turn them into a full polite question. Now we go through all five cards. First ask yourself, then you hear a model question and the examiner’s answer.

4
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:47,008
Card 1: You are at the post office.

5
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:50,533
You are at the post office. You want to send a parcel abroad.

6
00:00:51,733 --> 00:00:54,228
Good afternoon. How can I help you?

7
00:01:00,433 --> 00:01:04,186
Hello, I want to send a parcel to Ukraine. How much does it cost?

8
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:07,833
A parcel up to 5 kilograms costs 650 CZK.

9
00:01:14,033 --> 00:01:15,383
How long does it take?

10
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:17,359
The parcel will be there in about five days.

11
00:01:23,567 --> 00:01:25,187
Can I pay by card?

12
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:28,094
Yes, you can pay by card or in cash.

13
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:36,033
Can I track the parcel online?

14
00:01:36,233 --> 00:01:38,789
Yes, you will find the tracking number on the receipt.

15
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Thank you for the information. Goodbye.

16
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,967
You're welcome. Goodbye.

17
00:01:44,167 --> 00:01:47,305
Card 2: You are at a language school.

18
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:51,395
You are at a language school. You want to sign up for an English course.

19
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,095
Good afternoon. How can I help you?

20
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:03,863
Hello, when does the English course start?

21
00:02:04,067 --> 00:02:06,167
The new course starts on 1 October.

22
00:02:12,367 --> 00:02:13,400
How much is it?

23
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:16,561
The course costs 4,500 CZK per term.

24
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:24,554
How many people are in the group?

25
00:02:24,767 --> 00:02:27,189
There are at most ten people in the group.

26
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,533
Is the course in the evening?

27
00:02:34,733 --> 00:02:37,652
Yes, the lessons are always on Tuesday at 6 pm.

28
00:02:37,867 --> 00:02:40,867
Thank you for the information. Goodbye.

29
00:02:41,067 --> 00:02:42,833
You're welcome. Goodbye.

30
00:02:43,033 --> 00:02:46,075
Card 3: You are at the doctor’s reception.

31
00:02:46,367 --> 00:02:50,191
You are at the doctor's reception. You want to book a check-up.

32
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:53,895
Good afternoon. How can I help you?

33
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:03,267
Hello, do you have a free slot for a check-up?

34
00:03:03,467 --> 00:03:05,330
We have a free slot on Thursday.

35
00:03:11,533 --> 00:03:13,067
What time can I come?

36
00:03:13,267 --> 00:03:15,033
You can come at ten.

37
00:03:21,233 --> 00:03:22,460
What should I bring?

38
00:03:22,667 --> 00:03:24,333
Bring your health insurance card.

39
00:03:30,533 --> 00:03:32,000
Do I have to come on an empty stomach?

40
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:35,589
No, you don't, you can have breakfast as usual.

41
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:38,800
Thank you for the information. Goodbye.

42
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,767
You're welcome. Goodbye.

43
00:03:40,967 --> 00:03:44,109
Card 4: You are at the station ticket office.

44
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:47,952
You are at the station ticket office. You want to take a train to Brno.

45
00:03:49,167 --> 00:03:51,661
Good afternoon. How can I help you?

46
00:03:57,867 --> 00:04:00,367
Hello, when is the train to Brno?

47
00:04:00,567 --> 00:04:02,899
The next train leaves at 10:15.

48
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:10,500
How much is the ticket?

49
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:12,633
The ticket costs 320 crowns.

50
00:04:18,833 --> 00:04:20,333
Do I have to change trains?

51
00:04:20,533 --> 00:04:22,033
No, the train is direct.

52
00:04:28,233 --> 00:04:30,033
Which platform does the train leave from?

53
00:04:30,233 --> 00:04:32,557
The train leaves from platform 3.

54
00:04:32,767 --> 00:04:35,767
Thank you for the information. Goodbye.

55
00:04:35,967 --> 00:04:37,367
Have a good trip.

56
00:04:37,567 --> 00:04:40,728
Card 5: You are in a clothes shop.

57
00:04:41,033 --> 00:04:44,914
You are in a clothes shop. You want to buy a winter jacket.

58
00:04:46,100 --> 00:04:48,595
Good afternoon. How can I help you?

59
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:58,064
Hello, do you have this jacket in a bigger size?

60
00:04:58,267 --> 00:05:00,500
Yes, we also have it in size L.

61
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:07,733
How much is it?

62
00:05:07,933 --> 00:05:10,333
The jacket costs 2,490 crowns.

63
00:05:16,533 --> 00:05:18,633
Can I return it if I don't like it?

64
00:05:18,833 --> 00:05:20,992
You can return it within 30 days.

65
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:28,788
Do you have it in black too?

66
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,327
Yes, we have black in all sizes.

67
00:05:31,533 --> 00:05:34,533
Thank you for the information. Goodbye.

68
00:05:34,733 --> 00:05:36,126
Thank you, goodbye.

69
00:05:36,333 --> 00:05:42,316
Now twelve questions that fit almost every card. Listen and repeat out loud.

70
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,185
How much does it cost?

71
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,700
When does the course start?

72
00:05:51,900 --> 00:05:53,700
What time are you open?

73
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:58,250
How long does it take?

74
00:06:01,467 --> 00:06:03,100
Where is the nearest stop?

75
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:08,360
Do you have this jacket in a bigger size?

76
00:06:11,567 --> 00:06:13,187
Can I pay by card?

77
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:17,900
Do I have to change trains?

78
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,733
What do I have to bring with me?

79
00:06:25,933 --> 00:06:27,400
Is it possible to return it?

80
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:32,267
How do I get to the station?

81
00:06:35,467 --> 00:06:38,033
Could you tell me where the ticket office is?

82
00:06:41,233 --> 00:06:44,292
Five typical mistakes that cost people points.

83
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:53,785
Correct: Kolik to stojí? Don’t just read the word from the card. Ask a full question.

84
00:06:57,500 --> 00:07:04,894
Correct: Můžu platit kartou? You must ask, not state. A question ends with a question mark.

85
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:15,424
Correct: Máte volný termín? With the examiner you speak formally: máte, můžete.

86
00:07:19,133 --> 00:07:27,285
Correct: Kdy jede vlak do Brna? Put the question word first: kdy, kde, kolik.

87
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:40,056
Correct: Je tam parkoviště? Prepare the fourth question in advance. Good ones: Je tam parkoviště? Můžu přijít i v sobotu?

88
00:07:41,267 --> 00:07:59,315
Summary. First: turn the hint into a full question. Second: speak formally — máte, můžete. Third: put the question word first. And fourth: have your own question ready.

89
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:10,657
Which card is the hardest for you? Write it in the comments. And if the video helped, give it a like — it helps others preparing for the exam.

90
00:08:11,867 --> 00:08:28,179
On the Zkouška A2 nanečisto website you can practise all cards for free — it listens and checks your question. Link in the description. Tomorrow: big review of Speaking task 3. Subscribe so you don’t miss anything.
